>> title: Harira
>> category: Soups
>> tags: lamb, lentils, chickpeas, moroccan, stovetop
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, One Pot
>> aka: hareera, harira soup, Moroccan lentil and chickpea soup, Ramadan soup
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 45 min

>> step: brown 8 min
Brown @lamb shoulder{1%lb}(450 g; cubed) in a #Dutch oven{} in its own fat for ~{8%min}.

>> step: sweat 8 min
Sweat @&(~1)lamb{} for ~{8%min} with @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped) and @celery{2%ribs}(chopped with their leaves).

>> step: toast 1 min
Toast @&(~1)base{} for ~{1%min} with @ground turmeric{1%tsp}(or a pinch of saffron) and @ground ginger{1%tsp}.

>> step: simmer 1 hr
Simmer @&(~1)base{} for ~{60%min} with @canned crushed tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g), @chickpeas{15%oz}(425 g; drained), @brown lentils{1/2%cup}(100 g), and @chicken stock{7%cups}(1.7 L).

>> step: cook 5 min, lemon at the table
Cook @&(~1)harira{} for ~{5%min} with @broken vermicelli{1/3%cup}(40 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, and @cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped), and pass @lemon wedges{12}(from 2 lemons) at the table.
